From: WelsonJS
Subject: [PATCH] llama : use the original chat template for BitNet b1.58 2B-4T

microsoft/BitNet-b1.58-2B-4T-gguf embeds the chat template
"Human: ...\n\nBITNETAssistant: ", which the model does not follow: through
/v1/chat/completions it invents a conversation instead of answering. The
original model (microsoft/bitnet-b1.58-2B-4T, tokenizer_config.json) uses
"User: ...<|eot_id|>Assistant: ".

Like the existing one-off fix for Mistral-Small-2503 in the same function,
return the original template when the architecture is bitnet-b1.58 and the
embedded template contains "BITNETAssistant". A template given with
--chat-template or --chat-template-file still takes precedence.

Apply with: git -c core.autocrlf=false apply <this file>

diff --git a/src/llama-model.cpp b/src/llama-model.cpp
index 6eda8f3..150be24 100644
--- a/src/llama-model.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-model.cpp
@@ -2651,6 +2651,15 @@ const char * llama_model_chat_template(const llama_model * model, const char * n
         return nullptr;
     }
 
+    // microsoft/BitNet-b1.58-2B-4T-gguf embeds a "Human: ... BITNETAssistant: " template,
+    // which the model does not follow; use the template of the original model
+    // (microsoft/bitnet-b1.58-2B-4T tokenizer_config.json) instead.
+    if (!name && model->arch == LLM_ARCH_BITNET_B158 && it->second.find("BITNETAssistant") != std::string::npos) {
+        return "{% set loop_messages = messages %}{% for message in loop_messages %}"
+               "{% set content = message['role'] | capitalize + ': '+ message['content'] | trim + '<|eot_id|>' %}"
+               "{{ content }}{% endfor %}{% if add_generation_prompt %}{{ 'Assistant: ' }}{% endif %}";
+    }
+
     return it->second.c_str();
 }
 
